WEBVTT

00:03.100 --> 00:05.600
Takumi, I apologize for the wait.

00:05.600 --> 00:06.360
Not a problem.

00:07.820 --> 00:09.160
That mark...

00:10.010 --> 00:13.050
<i>The sunken ship I cleaned up 
at the mermaids' village!</i>

00:13.880 --> 00:16.060
<i>I think its name was...</i>

00:16.990 --> 00:20.650
Mr. Cedric, have you heard of the <i>Dietlinde</i>?

00:20.650 --> 00:22.460
The <i>Dietlinde</i>...

00:22.890 --> 00:26.220
I do recall reading about it 
in a report not long ago...

00:26.220 --> 00:30.460
Oh, wasn't that the name of a 
merchant ship of yours that sank?

00:30.460 --> 00:32.000
Yes, it was.

00:32.000 --> 00:34.380
Thankfully, there were no casualties,

00:34.380 --> 00:36.390
but it was still quite a blow.

00:36.390 --> 00:37.390
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:37.780 --> 00:41.650
Actually, I recovered the <i>Dietlinde</i>.

00:44.000 --> 00:46.020
What? The ship sank, sir.

00:46.310 --> 00:48.480
Yes. I found it at the bottom of the ocean.

00:48.760 --> 00:52.490
Hm? But it was well off the coast...

00:52.920 --> 00:55.650
I-I was doing a bit of 
long-distance swimming...

00:56.110 --> 00:59.370
But I'm certain that ship was quite large...

00:59.370 --> 01:02.080
It was. It's in my inventory.

01:03.520 --> 01:06.790
And what is it you wish to do with this ship?

01:07.090 --> 01:10.000
Huh? Wouldn't returning it 
be the normal thing to do?

01:10.000 --> 01:12.680
Returning the ship to its owner?

01:12.680 --> 01:13.510
Yes.

01:13.770 --> 01:15.640
Some of the cargo was still in it,

01:15.640 --> 01:18.720
so I figured it must 
have been quite a big loss.

01:18.720 --> 01:21.710
I don't know what kind of shape it's all in,

01:21.710 --> 01:23.740
but some of it might be salvageable.

01:24.970 --> 01:28.440
Are you saying you'll return it 
with no expectation of payment?

01:28.440 --> 01:31.020
Huh? Isn't that how it normally works?

01:32.180 --> 01:34.990
<i>Did I say something to confuse them?</i>

01:43.370 --> 01:49.630
<b>A Journey Through Another World: 
Raising Kids While Adventuring</b>

03:05.450 --> 03:09.960
<b>Vector Does a Good Job!</b>

03:06.160 --> 03:08.630
<i>After that, Mr. Cedric and 
the branch owner informed me</i>

03:08.630 --> 03:13.380
<i>that when someone finds something in 
this world, they become its owner.</i>

03:13.770 --> 03:17.120
<i>The same goes for stolen 
goods recovered from bandits.</i>

03:17.120 --> 03:20.360
<i>Ownership is transferred to 
whoever defeats the bandits.</i>

03:20.360 --> 03:22.790
<i>If the previous owner wants their stuff back,</i>

03:22.790 --> 03:25.850
<i>they have to buy it back after 
negotiating compensation.</i>

03:25.850 --> 03:28.500
Sorry. I'm from the countryside, 
so I don't know these things.

03:28.500 --> 03:32.350
Oh, not at all! I genuinely don't 
know how we can ever thank you!

03:32.900 --> 03:35.850
The large fairy stone that powered that ship

03:35.850 --> 03:38.280
was extremely valuable, you see.

03:38.710 --> 03:42.960
The ship sank because its underside 
was damaged, causing it to flood.

03:42.960 --> 03:45.630
The fairy stone itself should be unharmed,

03:45.630 --> 03:49.250
so if we can recover it, it'll go a 
long way in making up for our losses.

03:49.600 --> 03:51.250
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

03:51.920 --> 03:55.500
You'll probably want to check 
the cargo first, right?

03:55.500 --> 03:58.550
Yes. Would you mind showing me at the harbor?

03:58.550 --> 03:59.690
It's this way.

03:59.690 --> 04:00.210
Sure.

04:00.510 --> 04:03.180
Taku, where are you going?

04:04.160 --> 04:07.270
Do you remember that sunken ship we found?

04:07.270 --> 04:08.270
Ship?

04:08.270 --> 04:09.100
Yeah.

04:09.530 --> 04:13.060
The one Millena and the other 
mermaids asked me to move.

04:13.340 --> 04:15.060
Yeah! We remember!

04:15.410 --> 04:19.820
We found out who lost it, 
so I'm going to return it to them.

04:20.240 --> 04:21.210
Return it?

04:21.210 --> 04:21.990
Why?

04:21.990 --> 04:23.660
Huh? "Why"?

04:24.130 --> 04:25.950
Well, um...

04:26.240 --> 04:31.120
If someone walking in front of you 
dropped something, what would you do?

04:31.120 --> 04:31.950
Pick it up?

04:31.950 --> 04:35.330
Right. And after that?

04:38.000 --> 04:39.090
Give it to them?

04:39.400 --> 04:41.120
I'm doing the same thing.

04:41.120 --> 04:45.010
I picked up their ship, and now 
I'm giving it back to its owner.

04:45.010 --> 04:46.050
Oh!

04:46.050 --> 04:47.190
Giving back...

04:47.190 --> 04:48.550
...their ship!

04:52.000 --> 04:56.140
<i>If they ever find anything someone 
lost, I hope they give it back.</i>

05:01.000 --> 05:02.060
Inventory.

05:15.020 --> 05:17.390
This is it. Can you confirm it's yours?

05:17.390 --> 05:19.420
Th-There's no doubt about it!

05:19.420 --> 05:21.420
This is our ship!

05:21.420 --> 05:23.130
Wow!

05:23.610 --> 05:26.210
Then shall we say it's been returned now?

05:26.210 --> 05:28.590
Yes! Thank you so much!

05:29.660 --> 05:32.510
<i>After that, having befriended 
the Fiji Trading Company,</i>

05:32.510 --> 05:34.980
<i>they showed me some of their merchandise.</i>

05:36.540 --> 05:37.280
Are these...

05:37.280 --> 05:39.400
Those are kawfi beans.

05:39.760 --> 05:41.140
Kawfi beans?

05:41.650 --> 05:43.750
<i>According to what Syl taught me...</i>

05:43.750 --> 05:46.510
The beans themselves are not fit for eating,

05:46.510 --> 05:49.370
but you can drink the liquid 
that's extracted from them.

05:49.730 --> 05:51.330
<i>Which means...</i>

05:51.740 --> 05:54.790
<i>These are coffee beans, aren't they?!</i>

05:55.090 --> 05:57.010
Thank you very much.

05:57.010 --> 05:59.400
I can finally have coffee again!

06:03.580 --> 06:05.670
Hey! These are...

06:06.360 --> 06:09.680
Turmeric, cardamom, coriander, and cloves!

06:10.170 --> 06:14.080
That's a port town for you! 
Trade in Bailey is definitely thriving!

06:15.060 --> 06:19.040
<i>Apparently, spices are used to 
make medicines in this world,</i>

06:19.040 --> 06:22.060
<i>but most of them seem to have the 
same names they did in my old world.</i>

06:22.060 --> 06:24.780
Well, there's only one thing 
to do with all these...

06:24.780 --> 06:26.900
And that's curry!

06:26.900 --> 06:27.740
Curry?

06:28.210 --> 06:30.450
It's a really tasty food.

06:31.440 --> 06:33.870
I really want some curry right about now!

06:33.870 --> 06:35.370
We do, too!

06:35.660 --> 06:38.750
I don't know how it'll turn 
out, but let's give it a shot!

06:38.750 --> 06:40.040
Give it a shot!

06:46.420 --> 06:50.120
<i>Mr. Cedric said we could borrow his kitchen,</i>

06:50.120 --> 06:52.390
<i>but we used the yard so 
the smell wouldn't stick.</i>

06:52.840 --> 06:55.200
Start by cutting toonions—which 
are like onions—

06:55.200 --> 06:57.890
and maro potatoes and carrots 
into bite-size pieces.

06:58.430 --> 07:00.810
Since we don't have pork, we'll use Orc meat.

07:01.330 --> 07:02.860
Cut it up and sauté it.

07:03.630 --> 07:06.730
Once it's cooked, we add it 
to our finished soup stock,

07:06.730 --> 07:09.050
and let it stew until the 
vegetables are cooked through.

07:09.050 --> 07:10.200
Let it stew!

07:10.470 --> 07:13.540
In the meantime, we'll put oil 
and flour in the frying pan

07:13.540 --> 07:17.200
along with our desired combination 
of spices to make the roux.

07:17.800 --> 07:21.120
Once it becomes fragrant, add some 
liquid from the veggie broth to it,

07:21.120 --> 07:23.040
then pour it all into the pot.

07:23.040 --> 07:24.290
We'll stir it!

07:24.610 --> 07:26.250
Okay, go for it.

07:26.580 --> 07:27.800
Stir, stir!

07:27.920 --> 07:29.210
Stir, stir!

07:29.210 --> 07:31.930
And now our secret ingredients.

07:31.930 --> 07:33.630
<b>Worcestershire
Sauce</b>

07:32.350 --> 07:36.220
<i>I like ketchup and Worcestershire 
sauce, but those don't exist here.</i>

07:36.220 --> 07:39.390
<i>Guess I'll go with the classic 
appe fruit and honey.</i>

07:39.690 --> 07:43.310
<i>A little sweetness will make it 
easier for Alan and Elena to eat.</i>

07:43.910 --> 07:47.850
Okay, now we just give it 
plenty of time to stew...

07:47.850 --> 07:49.320
but what say we cheat a bit?

07:49.320 --> 07:50.530
Cheat?

07:51.950 --> 07:54.900
<i>One of the time-space magic 
spells I learned recently</i>

07:54.900 --> 07:58.700
<i>makes time pass by more quickly 
for any object that isn't alive.</i>

08:00.230 --> 08:01.720
Aging!

08:01.720 --> 08:03.840
<i>Now it'll be done in an instant!</i>

08:05.170 --> 08:06.400
And it's ready!

08:06.400 --> 08:07.880
Yay!

08:11.370 --> 08:13.080
Oh, it's just right!

08:13.080 --> 08:15.280
Alan, Elena, open wide.

08:16.840 --> 08:18.720
How is it? Not too spicy?

08:18.720 --> 08:20.470
Yummy!

08:23.640 --> 08:25.940
What's wrong? Was it spicy after all?

08:25.940 --> 08:27.160
Over there.

08:27.160 --> 08:28.150
Lots.

08:29.580 --> 08:30.320
Whoa!

08:30.690 --> 08:34.610
<i>I guess all the staff in the 
mansion were drawn to the smell.</i>

08:34.610 --> 08:35.780
Takumi...

08:36.160 --> 08:37.850
What is this?

08:37.850 --> 08:40.740
It's a dish called curry, from my homeland.

08:40.740 --> 08:43.960
It smells great, but that's quite a color...

08:43.960 --> 08:46.460
It has a few medicinal herbs in it.

08:46.460 --> 08:48.880
They give it its color and aroma.

08:48.880 --> 08:50.120
Medicinal herbs?!

08:50.120 --> 08:52.980
I had no idea they could 
smell so appetizing...

08:52.980 --> 08:56.130
<i>Guess I'll put the tasting on hold 
and make enough for everyone.</i>

09:01.920 --> 09:02.770
This is...

09:02.770 --> 09:04.180
It's delicious!

09:04.180 --> 09:04.730
Mm!

09:04.730 --> 09:07.040
Taku, this is yummy!

09:07.040 --> 09:08.190
I'm glad.

09:08.990 --> 09:12.190
<i>I made this to go with the bread they 
provided for us at the mansion today,</i>

09:12.530 --> 09:16.700
<i>but once people learn about white 
wheat, I'd love to make curry rice.</i>

09:18.820 --> 09:21.280
<i>Curry really is great, though!</i>

09:21.280 --> 09:22.330
<i>I could die happy!</i>

09:22.760 --> 09:27.790
The jelly was good, too, but it's amazing 
that you can cook dishes like this, Takumi!

09:28.120 --> 09:30.000
Taku is amazing?

09:30.000 --> 09:31.330
Yeah! He is!

09:31.330 --> 09:32.960
He really <i>is</i> amazing!

09:32.960 --> 09:35.420
Yeah! Taku is amazing!

09:35.850 --> 09:40.340
<i>Oh, it looks like they're finally able 
to talk with Theodore and Latis now.</i>

09:41.120 --> 09:44.050
<i>Mr. Cedric is being awfully quiet, though.</i>

09:44.050 --> 09:44.890
Takumi...

09:44.890 --> 09:46.300
Y-Yes?

09:47.820 --> 09:50.930
This dish you call "curry" 
is an absolute marvel!

09:50.930 --> 09:52.950
Such a complex, yet refined flavor!

09:52.190 --> 09:53.860
<i>Uh, what now?</i>

09:52.950 --> 09:55.520
And an aroma that stimulates 
the appetite without end!

09:53.860 --> 09:56.490
<i>This is not the quiet, 
peaceful Mr. Cedric I know.</i>

09:55.520 --> 09:59.450
They're all playing a beautiful 
harmony in my mouth!

09:57.440 --> 09:59.450
Father is acting strange...

09:59.450 --> 10:02.260
<i>Did I put something weird in the curry?</i>

10:02.260 --> 10:04.030
<i>I </i>did<i> use a lot of spices.</i>

10:04.030 --> 10:06.910
<i>Maybe one of them was 
some kind of stimulant...</i>

10:07.170 --> 10:08.170
Pardon me.

10:10.700 --> 10:12.880
What is it, Chef?

10:12.880 --> 10:14.510
My apologies, sir.

10:14.510 --> 10:16.670
I realize I'm being rude,

10:16.670 --> 10:19.930
but after tasting that dish, 
I just couldn't sit still.

10:20.280 --> 10:21.540
Sir Takumi!

10:21.540 --> 10:24.960
I also partook of this "curry" 
dish that you've made!

10:24.960 --> 10:25.890
Uh, okay...

10:26.350 --> 10:28.800
This dish known as curry is wondrous!

10:28.800 --> 10:31.330
I've been cooking for many years,

10:31.330 --> 10:34.110
but this is the first time any dish 
has left such an impact on me!

10:34.540 --> 10:36.960
Please take me as your apprentice!

10:36.960 --> 10:37.610
Huh?!

10:37.610 --> 10:40.380
Sorry, but I don't think...

10:40.380 --> 10:43.040
Why not?! Are my skills insufficient?!

10:43.040 --> 10:44.530
Cooking has been my life for—

10:44.000 --> 10:45.500
Please, Ryan.

10:45.500 --> 10:48.500
Don't make things awkward for Takumi.

10:48.500 --> 10:51.680
He's not a cook. he's an adventurer.

10:51.680 --> 10:53.500
He's not going to take an apprentice.

10:53.500 --> 10:55.380
But, sir...

10:55.730 --> 10:58.880
I do understand how you feel, though.

10:59.510 --> 11:03.890
Cream bread, jelly, scallops with 
butter and soy sauce, and now curry...

11:04.350 --> 11:09.520
It's strange <i>not</i> to think of someone 
who invents so many dishes as a cook.

11:10.160 --> 11:12.650
Why not change jobs and become a cook now?

11:12.650 --> 11:14.520
And then take me as your apprentice!

11:14.520 --> 11:15.610
I'm not doing that!

11:15.610 --> 11:17.360
You're gonna be a cook?

11:17.360 --> 11:18.570
No, I'm not.

11:19.570 --> 11:21.600
The curry really was delicious!

11:21.600 --> 11:23.030
Thank you!

11:23.440 --> 11:27.250
I know you've been on many adventures.

11:27.250 --> 11:29.200
What sorts of monsters have you defeated?

11:29.200 --> 11:31.250
What are labyrinths like?

11:31.250 --> 11:34.210
You two are interested in that stuff?

11:34.210 --> 11:34.960
Yes!

11:34.960 --> 11:39.620
I love stories about going on adventures 
and slaying dragons and such!

11:39.620 --> 11:40.470
Me, too!

11:40.470 --> 11:41.670
I see.

11:41.670 --> 11:45.680
Then how about a story of the monsters 
I defeated near the town of Shireen?

11:45.950 --> 11:47.530
Tell us! Tell us!

11:48.540 --> 11:53.710
It happened when they created a force of 
knights and adventurers to slay monsters.

11:55.260 --> 12:01.030
<i>So I told the boys about the many monsters 
we defeated in the forest around Shireen.</i>

12:05.390 --> 12:06.240
Wow!

12:06.240 --> 12:11.460
Isn't it dangerous for Alan and 
Elena to go adventuring with you?

12:11.810 --> 12:15.280
Ah... Well, there is certainly danger,

12:15.280 --> 12:17.420
but Alan and Elena are strong.

12:17.420 --> 12:18.640
They are?

12:18.640 --> 12:19.840
They are.

12:19.840 --> 12:21.460
Stronger than a wolf?

12:21.460 --> 12:22.550
Or a goblin?

12:22.880 --> 12:26.050
They can easily take down a wolf or a goblin.

12:26.960 --> 12:27.800
Wow!

12:28.160 --> 12:29.750
They're incredible for such little kids!

12:29.420 --> 12:33.230
Hear that, Alan, Elena? 
They're saying how amazing you are.

12:29.750 --> 12:30.940
So cool!

12:30.940 --> 12:33.230
I know, right?

12:35.690 --> 12:37.690
<i>Wait, is this...</i>

12:39.220 --> 12:42.270
I guess your praise made them 
so happy, they got all shy.

12:42.270 --> 12:43.760
Really?

12:43.760 --> 12:44.920
Yep. Right?

12:46.490 --> 12:48.660
You're amazing!

12:51.880 --> 12:53.370
<i>And then, the next day,</i>

12:53.370 --> 12:56.330
<i>the three of us plus Theodore and Latis</i>

12:56.330 --> 12:59.540
<i>went to visit the Risner 
family's favorite bakery.</i>

12:59.820 --> 13:04.200
<i>I taught them how to make cream and red 
bean paste Mr. Cedric had asked for,</i>

13:04.200 --> 13:06.970
<i>and asked them on his behalf to 
make some new types of bread.</i>

13:07.410 --> 13:10.000
Here are the recipes. Which should we make?

13:10.000 --> 13:12.160
I want to make curry bread!

13:12.160 --> 13:14.620
I want kawfi cream bread!

13:15.590 --> 13:17.120
Let's make it together, Alan!

13:17.120 --> 13:18.540
Okay!

13:18.540 --> 13:20.110
I'll work with you, Elena!

13:20.110 --> 13:21.150
Okay!

13:21.660 --> 13:23.920
Press, press...

13:23.920 --> 13:25.110
Just like that.

13:25.360 --> 13:26.450
Try it, Alan.

13:26.450 --> 13:27.070
Okay!

13:27.440 --> 13:29.140
Press, press...

13:29.350 --> 13:31.030
Press, press...

13:34.560 --> 13:37.460
Okay, the cream is looking good.

13:37.460 --> 13:40.480
Now we just put this in the baked buns.

13:40.480 --> 13:41.670
Okay!

13:48.320 --> 13:49.540
That's okay.

13:50.760 --> 13:51.970
There, all better.

13:52.320 --> 13:53.680
Oh, good!

13:54.690 --> 13:56.050
Oh, your cheek!

13:56.050 --> 13:57.390
Powder!

13:57.650 --> 13:59.290
Huh? I got some on me?

13:59.290 --> 14:00.360
Where? Where?

14:00.620 --> 14:02.330
You spread it around!

14:02.330 --> 14:03.320
Huh?!

14:07.170 --> 14:11.990
<i>I invited the boys because it seemed like 
Alan and Elena had warmed up to them a bit,</i>

14:12.520 --> 14:15.910
<i>but they're doing great, 
talking to kids their own age now.</i>

14:16.450 --> 14:20.130
Kawfi Cream Bread

14:16.960 --> 14:21.010
<i>A cream bread with the liquid from 
kawfi beans mixed in the cream.</i>

14:20.130 --> 14:24.050
Curry Bread

14:21.010 --> 14:23.780
<i>Curry bread with keema curry filling.</i>

14:23.780 --> 14:28.430
<i>Tuna and onion bread with mayonnaise, 
tuna, and finely chopped toonions.</i>

14:24.050 --> 14:28.430
Tuna and Onion Bread

14:28.640 --> 14:31.200
I think they turned out well.

14:31.200 --> 14:32.690
They all look delicious!

14:32.690 --> 14:33.980
Yummy!

14:33.980 --> 14:37.850
Alan, Elena, you haven't tried them 
yet, so you mean they <i>look</i> yummy.

14:38.130 --> 14:39.430
They look yummy!

14:39.430 --> 14:40.350
That's right.

14:42.120 --> 14:43.230
It's so good!

14:43.520 --> 14:45.290
They're all the best!

14:46.160 --> 14:47.900
Yeah! The best!

14:52.880 --> 14:55.400
Boss, these are perfectly baked.

14:55.400 --> 14:56.280
Takumi!

14:56.280 --> 14:57.370
Y-Yes?

14:57.700 --> 14:59.550
These are all incredible!

14:59.550 --> 15:01.370
Please take me as your apprentice!

15:01.790 --> 15:02.920
I won't be doing that.

15:02.920 --> 15:03.840
Aww!

15:05.400 --> 15:07.800
Our chef, Ryan, said the same thing!

15:08.180 --> 15:09.760
He did!

15:10.000 --> 15:11.720
He did!

15:13.530 --> 15:15.560
Let's make bread together again sometime!

15:15.560 --> 15:18.140
We'll make a whole bunch next 
time! More than we can eat!

15:18.400 --> 15:19.770
Yeah! We will!

15:19.770 --> 15:21.600
Lots! Bunches!

15:21.600 --> 15:24.700
We'll make kawfi cream 
bread and red bean buns...

15:24.700 --> 15:25.820
And curry bread, too!

15:26.500 --> 15:28.100
<i>A few days later,</i>

15:28.100 --> 15:32.280
<i>we were just outside town on our 
way to visit a nearby mountain.</i>

15:33.000 --> 15:34.990
Guys, you can come out.

15:38.470 --> 15:39.410
You guys!

15:39.740 --> 15:43.890
There's a small mountain about 
a half day's walk from here.

15:43.890 --> 15:46.880
I'd like to go see it. How about all of you?

15:46.880 --> 15:48.590
Let's go!

15:48.900 --> 15:52.800
Joule, Feat, can I ask you guys to carry us?

15:52.800 --> 15:54.200
<i>Of course!</i>

15:52.800 --> 15:54.200
<i>Leave it to us!</i>

15:57.110 --> 16:00.800
Huh? Do you want to give 
us a ride too, Vector?

16:03.050 --> 16:07.680
<i>You can't! It's </i>our<i> job to 
carry Taku and the kids!</i>

16:07.680 --> 16:09.990
<i>You just keep quiet, Vector.</i>

16:13.170 --> 16:15.160
I think they're arguing...

16:15.430 --> 16:17.120
They're arguing.

16:17.660 --> 16:20.220
<i>Feat doesn't seem interested.</i>

16:20.850 --> 16:24.160
All right, then we'll ride 
on Joule and Feat today.

16:24.160 --> 16:25.930
Vector, some other time, okay?

16:27.090 --> 16:29.390
<i>Frankly, if we ride on Vector,</i>

16:29.390 --> 16:32.050
<i>I'm afraid he'll go crazy and throw us off.</i>

16:32.050 --> 16:33.670
Okay, let's go!

16:33.670 --> 16:35.010
Let's go!

16:40.160 --> 16:42.400
Looks like the path gets narrower here.

16:43.640 --> 16:47.550
Joule and Feat, it'll probably be easier 
for you to travel if you're smaller.

16:48.140 --> 16:49.030
<i>Yeah.</i>

16:49.030 --> 16:50.270
<i>Okay, then.</i>

16:54.740 --> 16:58.530
Vector's already as small as he gets, 
so there's not much we can do there.

17:00.120 --> 17:03.120
I hope he doesn't get caught on 
any branches and hurt himself...

17:04.140 --> 17:05.580
Guess I don't need to worry.

17:09.010 --> 17:10.730
Well, what should we play?

17:10.730 --> 17:11.800
Medicinal herbs!

17:11.800 --> 17:13.300
Find some!

17:13.300 --> 17:15.760
Huh? You want to find medicinal herbs?

17:15.760 --> 17:19.100
We don't have a quest, 
so you can play if you want.

17:19.100 --> 17:20.190
We wanna search!

17:20.310 --> 17:21.970
<i>We wanna search!</i>

17:22.280 --> 17:24.460
Well, okay, then...

17:24.460 --> 17:27.690
Let's look for some herbs 
we can use for cooking.

17:27.970 --> 17:29.770
Yeah! Let's look!

17:30.670 --> 17:32.060
Alan? Elena?

17:33.180 --> 17:33.940
Detect.

17:36.980 --> 17:40.580
<i>Multiple presences... and they're 
not animals or monsters.</i>

17:41.080 --> 17:42.140
<i>This is...</i>

17:44.530 --> 17:45.420
<i>Appraise.</i>

17:45.580 --> 17:46.540
Status

17:46.860 --> 17:48.320
Bandits?!

17:48.320 --> 17:49.500
Hey, boss.

17:49.930 --> 17:52.600
It's a guy and two little kids.

17:52.600 --> 17:54.710
Hmph. No women?

17:54.710 --> 17:56.000
Okay, boys!

17:56.000 --> 17:58.330
Kill the guy and take 
anything valuable he has!

17:58.330 --> 18:00.430
But don't kill the kids. We can sell 'em.

18:00.740 --> 18:01.890
Got it.

18:02.340 --> 18:04.850
<i>I doubt there's any chance we can run away.</i>

18:05.630 --> 18:08.770
<i>These guys all seem more 
than ready to fight, but...</i>

18:09.200 --> 18:13.360
Alan, Elena, would you mind 
just leaving this to me?

18:13.360 --> 18:14.470
I'll fight 'em!

18:14.470 --> 18:15.280
Me, too!

18:16.080 --> 18:18.740
<i>They're not gonna back down, are they?</i>

18:18.740 --> 18:19.990
Okay, then...

18:20.270 --> 18:21.920
Can you go easy on them?

18:21.920 --> 18:23.950
I don't want anyone getting badly hurt.

18:23.950 --> 18:25.410
We can!

18:25.810 --> 18:26.930
You guys, too.

18:26.930 --> 18:28.020
<i>Okay!</i>

18:26.930 --> 18:28.020
<i>Got it!</i>

18:28.620 --> 18:31.430
What are you guys blabbin' about?

18:31.430 --> 18:33.630
Boys! Get 'em!

18:47.850 --> 18:51.300
<i>Is he trying harder to do well 
since I reined him in earlier?</i>

18:53.400 --> 18:56.670
What're you idiots <i>doing</i>?! Get it together!

19:02.450 --> 19:05.160
<i>Uh... He's still alive, right?</i>

19:05.760 --> 19:08.620
That was great, Vector! Good job!

19:08.900 --> 19:10.320
Good job!

19:10.320 --> 19:12.800
<i>We didn't even get a chance to do anything.</i>

19:12.800 --> 19:14.590
<i>You truly did a wonderful job!</i>

19:14.900 --> 19:18.010
<i>Well, it was pretty good, 
I guess. For Vector.</i>

19:18.780 --> 19:20.220
Okay, well...

19:20.220 --> 19:25.220
We could just go back to town and let 
the guild or the knights handle them...

19:25.910 --> 19:29.310
But that's a lot of work. 
It'd be faster to do it ourselves.

19:31.200 --> 19:34.500
Can you tell us where your base is?

19:34.500 --> 19:36.570
Hmph! I ain't tellin' you!

19:38.530 --> 19:40.530
I'll tell you! I'll tell you!

19:51.160 --> 19:52.620
Yeah, so then...

19:53.430 --> 19:55.990
Hey, you're lat—wait... Kids?

20:00.760 --> 20:02.440
Wh-Who the hell are you guys?!

20:06.630 --> 20:09.210
<i>All that praise made him 
want to try even harder.</i>

20:19.380 --> 20:20.780
Taku...

20:21.050 --> 20:22.240
Here.

20:23.500 --> 20:24.740
<i>What's</i> here?

20:29.430 --> 20:30.950
Treasure!

20:30.950 --> 20:33.370
I guess it's all stuff the bandits stole.

20:33.950 --> 20:36.060
Good job finding it, you two.

20:38.020 --> 20:39.080
Inventory.

20:40.800 --> 20:44.480
<i>I'll take it back and ask 
Mr. Cedric what we should do with it.</i>

20:45.290 --> 20:46.760
Taku...

20:47.080 --> 20:48.000
A dungeon?

20:48.000 --> 20:49.500
Someone's in there.

20:53.720 --> 20:57.660
<i>People? They were all 
captured by those bandits?</i>

20:58.480 --> 20:59.350
Excuse me...

21:00.110 --> 21:02.940
Oh, we're just adventurers.

21:02.940 --> 21:06.030
You can relax. We defeated the bandits.

21:06.030 --> 21:08.410
Y-You did?

21:08.410 --> 21:10.890
Yes. It's all right now.

21:12.310 --> 21:13.810
I'll open this up.

21:24.300 --> 21:25.430
I'm glad for them.

21:26.340 --> 21:28.090
Yeah! Glad!

21:28.940 --> 21:31.450
And thanks for keeping watch, you guys.

21:31.450 --> 21:34.400
<i>No problem! That part was easy!</i>

21:34.400 --> 21:35.060
<i>Yeah!</i>

21:35.350 --> 21:37.390
<i>Ask me for anything, bro!</i>

21:37.390 --> 21:38.390
Okay...

21:39.060 --> 21:40.020
Huh?

21:40.630 --> 21:42.820
Vector, was that... Telepathy?

21:42.820 --> 21:44.740
<i>Yep! I learned it!</i>

21:44.740 --> 21:49.240
Status

21:45.040 --> 21:48.800
I see. You learned the skill 
after defeating those bandits.

21:48.800 --> 21:49.740
<i>Bro!</i>

21:50.510 --> 21:54.690
<i>I beat all of them by myself! 
Wasn't I </i>awesome<i>?!</i>

21:54.690 --> 21:56.910
Oh, yeah... It was all thanks to you.

21:57.200 --> 21:59.580
<i>Bro! I'll do good next time, too!</i>

21:59.580 --> 22:01.630
<i>So praise me lots!</i>

22:01.630 --> 22:02.780
<i>Me, too!</i>

22:02.870 --> 22:03.840
<i>Me, too!</i>

22:03.840 --> 22:04.900
Me, too!

22:05.000 --> 22:06.050
Me, too!

22:06.050 --> 22:08.300
<i>Chief! Don't forget me!</i>

22:09.010 --> 22:11.420
<i>Looks like it's gonna be 
even livelier around here...</i>

23:44.900 --> 23:49.900
<b>Next Time</b>

23:45.400 --> 23:49.900
<b>Bye-Bye! See You Next Time!</b>

23:46.120 --> 23:48.860
"Bye-Bye! See You Next Time!"
